# What must never reach the build context for the API image.
#
# In force when the image is built with this directory as the context, which is
# how api/Dockerfile is meant to be built:  docker build -t medisense-api ./api

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# A .env copied into a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image, and
# stays readable after a later layer deletes it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- The developer's environment ---------------------------------------------
# Platform-specific, several hundred megabytes, and rebuilt inside the image
# anyway. Copying it in is also how a Windows binary ends up in a Linux image.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- OCR models --------------------------------------------------------------
# Downloaded on first use, and large.
.paddleocr/
.paddlex/

# --- Not part of a running API -----------------------------------------------
# `alembic/` is deliberately absent from this list: migrations ship with the
# image so `alembic upgrade head` can be run as a one-off against a deployment
# without needing a checkout of the repository beside it.
tests/
scripts/
Makefile.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# --- Editor / OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
